WEBVTT

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.360
"Kodomo no Odocha"

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:13.700
That rumor that I love you

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.330
is true, yes it is.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.830
You can't ignore it either.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.420
Whether you're awake or asleep,

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:29.050
please don't be embarrassed.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.590
Is it a sin if I sneak into your heart

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:40.310
by ridding you...

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:43.480
...of your other love?

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:48.060
At sunset,

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:50.570
when the children go home,

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:54.530
Today's incident is burning love!

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:58.410
You can tell it accurately.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.490
7 O'Clock News!

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:04.290
Please, our relationship...

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:09.960
Please don't blame it on the true kiss

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:11.800
In a city without light,

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:15.630
let's burn the fire of love.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:19.050
Don't be so easy going

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:21.350
The existence is a mistake

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.850
You're asking for something not there.

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:36.360
I'm Kurata Sana, a TV personality
with Gekidan Komawari, and 6th grader.

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:39.530
My beloved Mama is a famous
Aoki-award winning novelist.

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:41.700
The chipmunk on her head is Maro-chan.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.400
My former boyfriend, Sagami Rei-kun.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:46.370
Right now, he's earnestly on the way
to becoming a fine manager.

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:48.040
The mysterious white bat straight man.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.370
I'm Babbit.

00:01:49.370 --> 00:01:51.040
13 years old, according to some reports.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:53.370
Hayama Akito, my natural enemy.

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:56.710
Even so, right now, when I'm around him,
I'm relaxed for some reason.

00:01:56.710 --> 00:01:58.150
Brought together by a simple present,

00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:02.320
Tsuyoshi-kun and Aya-chan are getting
along great. Eh, but I'm not jealous!

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:07.320
And here's Tsuyoshi-kun's sister,
Aono-chan, a 2nd grader.

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:10.360
"Cock-a-Doodle-Doo, Morning is Coming"

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:27.410
Ah, Tsuyoshi-kun!

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:30.080
Good morning, Tsuyoshi-kun.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:33.350
Ah, it's you, Aya-chan. Good morning.

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:36.350
T- Tsuyoshi-kun, what's wrong with you!?

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:41.630
T- there's nothing
really wrong with me...

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:47.670
"Tsuyoshi-kun has collapsed"

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:54.030
Huh? Aya-chan, where am I?

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:59.030
The nurse's office. The nurse said
you could rest here for a bit.

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:01.040
Thanks.

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:05.710
Tsuyoshi-kun, by any chance,
is it because of this?

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:07.050
You got me.

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:11.050
Is there anything I can do?
Ask me anything, Tsuyoshi-kun.

00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:12.720
Thanks, Aya-chan.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:14.670
Tsuyoshi-kun...

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:19.390
It's 9 o'clock already.
Homeroom has begun.

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:23.230
Mm-hmm. I already
told Mitsuya-sensei, so it's okay.

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:25.060
They seemed to be
fired up about something.

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:26.730
Fired up?

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:27.440
"Soul-searching for this week"

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:31.670
Okay, Hisae-chan.

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:34.010
I'm troubled that some of the boys
immediately loaf around

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:35.010
during cleaning time.

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:36.680
Yeah! Yeah!

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:38.010
I'm troubled that some of the girls

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:41.680
yak it up and dawdle around
during cleaning time.

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:44.350
How are we supposed to hang around
with those oban hags?

00:03:44.350 --> 00:03:45.680
--What was that!?
--What was that!?

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:47.190
Who are you calling oban hags!?

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:49.020
I dare you to say that again,
you ojin stick-in-the-mud!

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:51.020
Go on, say it!

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:53.020
♪ Oban-ban-ban-ban-ban-ban! ♪

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:54.030
A bi-ban-non-non.

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:55.690
♪ Oban-ban-ban-ban-ban-ban! ♪

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:57.360
Brush your teeth!

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:59.360
Whose side are you on!?

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:02.180
I'm on Kato-chan's side!

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:06.040
Grade-schoolers are neither
ojin sticks-in-the-mud nor oban hags!

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:10.040
Okay, does anyone have anything to say
about themselves, and not just others?

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:11.380
Yes! Yes! Yes! Yes!

00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:12.710
Yes, Sana-chan?

00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:17.710
I was recently told by Zenjiro-sensei
"you're pretty sexy, awn't you?"

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:22.050
Don't be an ass! You call
that soul-searching?

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:25.720
Well, I don't have anything
I need to search my soul over.

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:27.930
What!? Get her!

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:32.660
Ka-ching!

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:35.330
Are you sure you shouldn't
still be resting?

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:38.440
Mm-mm, but still, I'll be fine.

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:43.010
Are you okay?

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:45.010
I just remembered it again.

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:47.350
You mean this?

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:48.350
This.

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:50.020
Say, what is "this"?

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:54.990
I can't leave it at home, but if I tried
to take it somewhere else, I'm sure...

00:04:56.360 --> 00:05:00.690
No, that can't happen!
Think of poor Aono-chan!

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:02.360
I don't know what I'm going to do.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:05.360
Why don't you talk to someone about it?

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:07.970
Oh, but don't tell Sana-chan.

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:11.040
If Sana-chan finds out,
I bet she'll really be concerned.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:12.440
Besides, if Sana-chan gets involved,

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:16.370
I have a feeling that things
will get much, much worse.

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:19.440
You got it. We won't tell Sana-chan.

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:22.050
I'll try to think of
any other ways to handle this.

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:24.050
Thanks, Aya-chan.

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:29.050
Hey, you two, we know that you're getting
along well and all, but what is "this"?

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:31.660
Tell Babbit!

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:34.990
Huh? Huh? Huh? Huh?

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:38.660
Come to think of it, I haven't seen
Aya-chan around today. Did she stay home?

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:39.870
She's in the nurse's office.

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:43.000
Tsuyoshi-kun wasn't feeling well,
so she said she would stay at his side.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:45.000
Eh!? Tsuyoshi-kun!?

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:53.350
Hayama! What did you do that for!?
Would you mind staying out of my way!?

00:05:53.350 --> 00:05:54.350
Don't.

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:57.680
Why not? After all, Tsuyoshi-kun is
in the nurse's office!

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:00.020
That's why I'm telling you to stop.

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:03.020
Huh? How come?

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:06.020
She's not too quick-witted...

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:08.690
Hisae-chan! Eri-chan, let's go
see how he's doing!

00:06:08.690 --> 00:06:11.030
No, that's okay. After all...

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:12.700
...you know?

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:15.980
Really? Well, I'll just pop on over.

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:20.710
I told you...

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:24.240
Come on, come on, you have spell it out
for her, or she won't understand.

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:26.710
Ba-bing, tell her, ba-bing.

00:06:26.710 --> 00:06:29.380
You'll be in the way.

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:30.980
In the way?

00:06:30.980 --> 00:06:34.320
Me? Why?

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:36.130
Dull-witted girl...

00:06:37.990 --> 00:06:40.990
Sana-chan, what are you doing?

00:06:40.990 --> 00:06:45.000
Tsuyoshi-kun! Are you okay?
I heard you weren't feeling well.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:48.000
Mm-hmm, I'm fine now.
Just a little anemia.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:52.670
Is that all? Don't go worrying
Aya-chan like that, lover-boy!

00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:54.170
Tsuyoshi-kun!

00:06:55.340 --> 00:06:57.010
Hey, Tsuyoshi,

00:06:57.010 --> 00:07:00.680
I heard you're raising a chicken
on the veranda of your apartment.

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:02.010
--Yikes!
--Yikes!

00:07:02.010 --> 00:07:03.350
Chicken?

00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:06.350
Oh, "this" was referring
to the chicken, was it?

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:09.420
Obana over in 1st Class said that it
makes a racket early in the morning,

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:11.360
and is making everyone angry.

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:14.460
Don't go keeping chickens
in your apartment!

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:19.030
Right, sorry...

00:07:19.030 --> 00:07:22.030
Say, Tsuyoshi-kun,
you're raising a chicken?

00:07:22.030 --> 00:07:23.900
Uh, well, you see...

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:26.370
--You're the one--
--A- Akito-kun!

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:28.710
...who gave them that chick, right?

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:30.040
Chick!?

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:31.780
"Could they mean...?"

00:07:31.980 --> 00:07:34.980
Aono-chan, what do you
have in your handbag?

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:36.310
An egg!

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:39.420
You know what? When you make
an egg warm, it turns into a chick.

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:40.320
Did you know that?

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:43.660
Say, is it actually some special egg
that a chick will hatch from?

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:47.660
Uh-uh, it's the regular kind they sell
at the supermarket in packs.

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:50.660
I snuck out at lunch recess
and bought it.

00:07:50.660 --> 00:07:52.660
Ah, Sana-chan!

00:07:52.670 --> 00:07:55.000
Ah! There are people watching us on TV!

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:56.710
Where? Where?

00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:04.680
It's been born! Aono's cute chick!

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:07.350
Yay! Yay!

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:11.500
It's the chick from back then.

00:08:18.690 --> 00:08:21.830
Yes, I gave it to her.

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:26.540
It has become a chicken.

00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:30.300
Wow, this is the chick from before?

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:33.300
But I feel sorry he
has to wear that mask.

00:08:33.310 --> 00:08:38.310
I made it last night and put it on,
but he takes it off by himself right away.

00:08:38.310 --> 00:08:40.280
This is what happens when you
give things to people willy-nilly

00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:41.650
without thinking first.

00:08:41.650 --> 00:08:43.980
I don't give things out willy-nilly!

00:08:43.980 --> 00:08:47.520
But last year, you did that
drive-by chocolating on Tsuyoshi-kun.

00:08:48.990 --> 00:08:50.630
Here! For you!

00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:55.160
But that was--

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:58.330
You're right, I did give it to him.

00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:03.330
Even so, Sana-chan, it's also true that
Aono was thrilled, and she adores it!

00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:09.450
I could keep it here forever, if it
wasn't for that crowing in the morning.

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:13.680
Shut up!

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:15.010
What time do you think it is!?

00:09:15.010 --> 00:09:17.020
Do something about that!

00:09:19.350 --> 00:09:21.350
Come on, Piyoko!

00:09:21.350 --> 00:09:24.360
What time do you think it is, anyway!?
We can't sleep, you know!

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:26.300
"I can't take it!"

00:09:28.030 --> 00:09:30.200
How about we cook it up and eat it?

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:33.630
Stop!

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:36.630
I'll manage something!

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:39.300
You'll manage something? What else
is there besides barbecue chicken?

00:09:39.310 --> 00:09:40.310
Huh?

00:09:40.310 --> 00:09:43.980
Oh, he's smart! Maybe we
can teach it some tricks.

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:46.310
Shake! Come on, shake.

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:47.980
Wow, he got it off, he got it off.

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:50.320
Can chickens do tricks?

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:51.980
Of course they can't.

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:53.990
The best they can do
is cook up nice and--

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:55.990
I'm home!

00:09:55.990 --> 00:09:57.930
Welcome back, Aono.

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:01.660
Huh? Aya-chan, and Sana-chan, too!

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:02.990
Hello.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:05.000
We've come to visit.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:06.330
Never mind you, Akito.

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:09.330
Say, did you see Aono's Piyoko?
He's gotten big, hasn't he?

00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:11.340
You're right!

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:14.010
Bawk, bawk, bawk.

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:17.010
Sana-chan, you're talking to Piyoko.

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:20.040
So, what will you do?
You told your neighbors

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:23.320
that you were going to do something
about this today, right?

00:10:30.620 --> 00:10:31.960
Aono...

00:10:31.960 --> 00:10:33.290
What?

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:37.630
Big Brother has a favor
to ask of you, Aono.

00:10:37.630 --> 00:10:40.500
Piyoko has gotten pretty big,

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:43.970
and I feel bad for keeping him
on this cramped veranda.

00:10:43.970 --> 00:10:46.970
So, I want Piyoko to go someplace where
he can run around more freely, and--

00:10:46.970 --> 00:10:48.640
No!

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:49.970
Aono...

00:10:49.980 --> 00:10:53.580
We can't keep Piyoko here.
There are lots of other people

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:56.650
living in these apartments.
It's like one big house, you see.

00:10:56.650 --> 00:10:58.780
When Piyoko crows as loud as he does,

00:10:58.780 --> 00:11:01.320
it wakes everyone up,
and they can't sleep.

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:04.660
Well, could we keep him
at our old house?

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:08.500
I'm going home to our old house!
I'm going home with Piyoko!

00:11:10.330 --> 00:11:12.900
You can't go back to
your old house, either.

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:16.330
And anyhow, this isn't even the chick
from the egg you were keeping warm--

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:18.540
Hayama!

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:22.010
What the hell are you doing?

00:11:22.010 --> 00:11:25.680
Say, Aono-chan,
I'll take Piyoko to my house.

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:29.010
That way, Aono-chan, you can come
see Piyoko any time you want,

00:11:29.010 --> 00:11:32.680
and it won't be any problem if Piyoko
crows a little at my house.

00:11:32.690 --> 00:11:34.020
Really?

00:11:34.020 --> 00:11:36.960
So, how about we ask her to
take him for a little while

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:39.360
until we can find
somewhere else to raise him?

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:42.360
Is it okay if Piyoko
stays over at my house?

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:45.700
Mm-hmm, if it's your house,
Sana-chan, that's fine.

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:48.370
You just don't learn from experience.

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:51.040
Huh? What? What do you mean by that?

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:52.700
Well, I've got karate.

00:11:52.710 --> 00:11:55.040
Hang on, Hayama...

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:57.110
Hayama...

00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:01.290
Apples! Apples!

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:13.870
This is Piyoko the rooster, who will be
staying with us briefly starting today,

00:12:13.870 --> 00:12:16.540
so I can take responsibility
for the lie I told.

00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:21.220
How many years has it been
since I've seen a chicken?

00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:24.550
I thought they died out a long time ago.

00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:27.640
You had some fried chicken
just this morning, didn't you?

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:31.520
Rei-kun! Rei-kun, that's a yellow card!

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:32.980
You are absolutely
forbidden to mention that,

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:34.190
especially in front of Aono!

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:35.520
Understood.

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:39.480
Sensei, are you done
with your manuscript yet?

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:44.240
Sensei! Please wake up! I've got
to deliver your manuscript tonight,

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:46.530
or I'll be fired!

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:49.540
So, what does a
live chicken eat, anyhow?

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:54.500
Well, you can give them corn,
and seashells, and broken china.

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:59.880
They really eat this sort of thing?

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:01.880
Onda, how do you know so much?

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:04.930
My parents have a farm
back in Higashimurayama,

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:06.890
and they keep chickens.

00:13:06.890 --> 00:13:09.890
I like you. I'll write for you.
Come along.

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:11.560
Thank you very much!

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:14.100
Sana, be sure to live up
to your responsibilities

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:15.230
and take care of that chicken.

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:16.230
Right.

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:17.560
It's like I'm dreaming!

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:18.560
Maybe you are.

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:20.230
Sensei...!

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:23.240
Sana-chan, where are you
going to keep this chicken?

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:26.160
Actually, we have a great place for him.

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:35.500
Ta-da! In here, the atrium
that Mama built for fun.

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:38.500
I get it. It's perfect in here, isn't it?

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:42.500
Okay, Piyoko, here's your new home.

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:46.090
Say, Rei-kun, do I do lots of things
without thinking them through,

00:13:46.090 --> 00:13:48.180
and cause problems for everyone else?

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:50.180
Huh? What brought that up
all of a sudden?

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:53.850
Am I a girl who doesn't
learn from experience?

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:58.190
I- I'm not sure I understand
your question, but Sana-chan,

00:13:58.190 --> 00:14:00.860
I think you're perfect
the way you are now.

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:03.820
Rei-kun, you always say that,

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:05.860
but the flak you get out in
the real world is harsh, isn't it?

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:09.110
Maybe I'll just live here with Piyoko.

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:15.870
Well done, Sana-chan. You might be able
to get the part of a chicken like that.

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:17.040
Huh?

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:23.420
Out of the way, Maro-chan.

00:14:26.220 --> 00:14:28.300
"Ah, I'm so tired..."

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:32.180
Mayumi...

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:34.470
My manuscript is done!

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:39.190
Nice work! Thank you very much!
Good night!

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:43.900
"Do not wake!! --Misako"

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:43.900
Don't you dare wake me up!

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:47.490
This is the first time all year that
I've had that refreshing feeling

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:48.820
of having done something nice.

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:50.950
Good night!

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:55.790
What!?

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:07.420
Why, you...!

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:11.590
--I said no one is
to wake me up, didn't I?
--Rei-kun, I'm scared.

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:14.510
Good morning!

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:15.890
Ah, Sana-chan.

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:18.560
Say, is Piyoko giving you any trouble?

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:21.020
No, everything's great!

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:38.500
Turns out I drew the
shortest straw of them all...

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:42.170
I'm begging you, be quiet, please!

00:15:42.170 --> 00:15:45.500
Ah, I slept well! I feel great now!

00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:47.840
Rei-kun!

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:49.840
I'm back, Rei-kun!

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:52.590
Welcome back, Sana-chan.
We've been waiting for you.

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:59.180
What's this, Sana-chan?
That's an awfully funny-looking baby!

00:15:59.180 --> 00:16:03.350
Hey, what part of my baby are you
calling funny-looking? How rude of you!

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:09.860
Cock-a-doodle-no-thank-you...

00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:14.870
♪ Piyoko the rooster
goes cock-a-doodle-doo. ♪

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:20.540
♪ He's too chipper, thank you,
I've had enough. ♪

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:26.540
♪ On the apartment's veranda,
cock-a-doodle-doo. ♪

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:32.550
♪ Here and there, everywhere,
cock-a-doodle-doo. ♪

00:16:33.470 --> 00:16:38.470
♪ Sana and Piyoko, que sera, sera. ♪

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:44.480
♪ And so, tomorrow as well,
cock-a-doodle-doo! ♪

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:49.480
Mm-hmm, I unduhstand. It's that
feeling of hawtrending loneliness, huh?

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:51.820
I'm the same way.

00:16:51.820 --> 00:16:54.820
Awtists are nevuh unduhstood, huh?

00:16:54.820 --> 00:16:56.740
Mm-hmm, let's both be strawng and foim,

00:16:56.740 --> 00:17:00.160
and go on living
without giving up, Sana-chan.

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:02.160
W- what is this!?

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:06.170
Huh? I wonder if Piyoko
likes you, Zenjiro-sensei.

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:08.250
What!? It's making me self-conscious

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:10.840
to have him stare at me
so intently like that.

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:14.840
Lately, giraffes and chickens have
stawted liking me for some reason.

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:17.180
That settles it!

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:19.850
Here on this auspicious day,

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:25.230
we would like to perform this
marriage for Piyoko. Drink up.

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:29.860
But Sana-chan,
isn't this chicken a roostuh?

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:33.320
No, no, Zenjiro-sensei,
even if he is a rooster,

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:34.820
as long as you love each other...

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:37.820
All right then, have a long
and happy life. Run away!

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:40.830
Hey, just a minute! Hey, Sana-chan,
you're not, by any chance,

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:42.160
trying to push this chicken on me,
are you!?

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:46.120
--Come get your roostuh!
Hey! Hold up! Hold up!
--Rei-kun! Rei-kun! Help, Rei-kun!

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:51.170
My plan to arrange a
marriage for Piyoko failed.

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:54.970
Everyone, we somehow managed
to get through the day.

00:18:03.850 --> 00:18:07.520
Shimura-san seems to be the
only one in a good mood, huh?

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:10.860
She said she used to raise around a
hundred chickens back home in the country.

00:18:10.860 --> 00:18:13.530
Well, let's not dwell too much on it.

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:15.860
Tomorrow's winds won't blow
until tomorrow, after all.

00:18:15.860 --> 00:18:17.530
"You never learn, Sana-chan"

00:18:15.860 --> 00:18:17.530
You never learn, do you?

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:27.540
Sana-chan, I said before that you
were perfect the way you were,

00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:30.540
but from now on, let's think
ahead a little more, okay?

00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:35.460
Can't you be any quieter
so early in the morning!?

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:37.260
"It's hopeless..."

00:18:41.470 --> 00:18:44.770
I can't take it anymore!!

00:18:45.810 --> 00:18:48.140
This is hopeless!

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:50.810
I'm coming for your cockscomb!

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:53.150
You can't!

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:56.820
Stand aside! We're going
to kill that thing!

00:18:56.820 --> 00:18:58.530
Anything but that!

00:18:58.530 --> 00:19:01.160
I will personally take the
responsibility for telling that lie!

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:03.830
Tsuyoshi-kun! Tsuyoshi-kun!

00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:05.950
Tsuyoshi-kun!

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:09.830
What? What? What's the matter?

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:12.830
Yes?

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:13.840
Huh?

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:16.510
Good afternoon. Is Piyoko here?

00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:18.630
Oh, if you're looking for the chicken,

00:19:18.630 --> 00:19:21.180
Sana-chan took it and ran away
from home a little while ago.

00:19:21.180 --> 00:19:22.800
--Ran away!?

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:30.190
Then, it was because of Piyoko?

00:19:30.190 --> 00:19:35.150
Sagami-kun went right after her, so I
think he'll find her soon. Don't worry.

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:38.650
She is the one who started all of
this in the first place, after all.

00:19:40.780 --> 00:19:42.490
Your head is funny!

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:43.780
Hey, Aono!

00:19:43.780 --> 00:19:45.830
Auntie looks like Piyoko!

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:47.830
It's okay, it's okay.

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:50.500
Lately, people have been getting
too used to my hairstyle as normal,

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:55.460
and nobody is surprised, or talks
about it anymore. I kind of miss it.

00:19:56.170 --> 00:19:58.130
It really is strange, isn't it?

00:19:58.130 --> 00:20:00.970
Look! I've got this one, too!

00:20:02.510 --> 00:20:04.800
Your hair is funny!

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:09.850
With this woman being Sana-chan's
mother and all, she really is amazing.

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:11.440
Thinking back on it now,

00:20:11.440 --> 00:20:15.190
I'm ashamed of myself for being
shaken up by a single chicken.

00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:19.530
I'll take in another 100 or
200 chickens, so bring them on over!

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:23.490
Actually, we found a place
that will take Piyoko for us.

00:20:23.490 --> 00:20:25.490
Huh? Really?

00:20:25.490 --> 00:20:28.330
Aya-chan found it for me.

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:35.960
Sana-chan, please, come on down!

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:38.800
We'll think of something for Piyoko
together one more time!

00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:41.800
There must be some
better way to handle this!

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:44.630
I've thought of a
million ways to handle it,

00:20:44.630 --> 00:20:46.470
and this is the one I ended up with.

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:49.470
In order for this chicken to have
a bright future, where he can crow,

00:20:49.470 --> 00:20:53.310
Sana is determined to fight
alongside Piyoko and Hachiko!

00:20:55.150 --> 00:20:59.150
Sana-chan... if you had
a monkey along, too, you'd be Momotaro.

00:20:59.150 --> 00:21:03.320
Momotaro had a pheasant that
accompanied him, not a chicken.

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:09.160
Yes, hello?

00:21:09.160 --> 00:21:10.830
Sensei?

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:12.160
Really!?

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:14.830
Sana-chan! We found it!

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:16.830
A place where Piyoko can crow!

00:21:16.830 --> 00:21:18.170
Huh!! Where!?

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:19.920
School!

00:21:21.840 --> 00:21:26.090
This week's Sana-chan!
There's a Momotaro feel to it.

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:28.760
Earlier, when we were cleaning,

00:21:28.760 --> 00:21:33.100
I was just casually passing by here,
and I thought to myself "Huh?"

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:38.060
So I asked Mitsuya-sensei, and she
said they used to keep a parrot here.

00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:42.110
Ever since the parrot died,
it has been unoccupied.

00:21:42.110 --> 00:21:45.780
Aya-chan made a request
to the principal for me.

00:21:47.410 --> 00:21:48.410
Right?

00:21:48.450 --> 00:21:50.490
Aya-chan, outstanding! Amazing!

00:21:50.490 --> 00:21:52.240
--Way to go! Good girl!
--This is what they call

00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:53.660
--Incredible! Outstanding!
--not knowing what's going on
in your own backyard, huh?

00:21:53.660 --> 00:21:54.750
Sana-chan...

00:21:54.790 --> 00:21:56.920
Ah, Aono-chan!

00:21:56.920 --> 00:21:58.580
Okay, Piyoko...

00:21:58.580 --> 00:22:01.590
This is your new home, Piyoko.

00:22:01.630 --> 00:22:05.340
The school is wide open, so you can
crow as loud and as much as you want.

00:22:05.340 --> 00:22:06.930
Good for you, Piyoko.

00:22:06.930 --> 00:22:10.260
Sana-chan, I'm sorry to put
you through all that trouble.

00:22:10.260 --> 00:22:12.930
You didn't put me to any trouble!

00:22:12.930 --> 00:22:15.810
You're one unlucky girl.

00:22:18.600 --> 00:22:22.650
And so, the affair was
more or less settled.

00:22:22.650 --> 00:22:24.940
Yaah!

00:22:24.940 --> 00:22:27.450
They say that chickens
will take three steps

00:22:27.450 --> 00:22:28.910
and forget whatever
it is they were told.

00:22:28.910 --> 00:22:33.660
But you are one fool who
will never learn, will you!?

00:22:40.710 --> 00:22:42.210
"Back against the wall."

00:22:42.710 --> 00:22:47.720
That's what you say about times like these.

00:22:48.970 --> 00:22:52.470
In dire straits,

00:22:53.220 --> 00:22:56.060
I've been waiting for an answer.

00:22:56.560 --> 00:22:59.940
My confessions are worked out
long in advance,

00:23:00.900 --> 00:23:05.030
to always go along with the scenario.

00:23:05.230 --> 00:23:11.070
My heart may be settled, but my mind is in a...

00:23:11.320 --> 00:23:13.280
...panic!!

00:23:14.330 --> 00:23:19.120
When my friends invite me by, suddenly,

00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:21.830
he's there.

00:23:22.750 --> 00:23:25.090
And our usual classroom...

00:23:25.300 --> 00:23:27.670
...quick-changes into a merry-go-round...

00:23:27.760 --> 00:23:30.180
...for two.

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:33.640
Although I've said nothing but wisecracks...

00:23:33.850 --> 00:23:38.390
...up to now, just for today,

00:23:39.310 --> 00:23:41.980
I'm going to be honest and sincere,

00:23:42.190 --> 00:23:46.690
so BOY, take a look my way!

00:23:47.610 --> 00:23:52.280
When my friends invite me by, suddenly,

00:23:52.450 --> 00:23:54.950
he's there,

00:23:55.910 --> 00:23:58.120
And our usual classroom...

00:23:58.370 --> 00:24:00.710
...quick-changes into a merry-go-round...

00:24:00.830 --> 00:24:03.210
...for two.

00:24:06.670 --> 00:24:09.670
Hoy! In Sana-chan's next adventures...

00:24:09.670 --> 00:24:11.680
He's back again! Mama's ex-husband!

00:24:11.680 --> 00:24:16.680
Eh? Ex-husband, a present for me?
Gapyon, the happy bunny? Bleh, how ugly!

00:24:16.680 --> 00:24:20.020
Ah, but still, I get to see a side of
her ex-husband that I never knew before.

00:24:20.020 --> 00:24:23.020
And then, Sana falls into the
devilish clutches of her ex-husband!

00:24:23.020 --> 00:24:26.940
Next time on Kodomo no Omocha,
Episode 27, the Whirlpool of Intrigue
in the Harbor District saga:

00:24:26.940 --> 00:24:30.610
Give Me Sympathy and Lend Me Money

00:24:30.610 --> 00:24:33.280
Elsewhere, what will
be Zenjiro-chan's fate,

00:24:33.280 --> 00:24:35.030
as he is caught up in it all?
